<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>

  <!-- Unlimited Blade Works, the Trace kit's ultimate. Granted by the Shirou Echo while manifested
       (AG_Echoes.xml, which also holds its charge cost). Casting it queues the chant (AG_UbwChant); UbwCast
       runs the rest. Every number is a placeholder (proposed 2026-09-24, taken as placeholders 2026-09-25).
       The cooldown is 2 days; it and the charge come back if the chant is stopped or broken before the
       release. -->
  <AbilityDef>
    <defName>AG_Trace_UnlimitedBladeWorks</defName>
    <label>unlimited blade works</label>
    <description>Chant up to three verses of 2 seconds. Press Release during a verse and the world opens when that verse ends; after the third verse it opens by itself.\n\nEveryone standing within 6, 9 or 12 cells (by verses said), allies and enemies alike, is taken into a 40 x 40 world of swords for 20, 25 or 30 seconds. Downed pawns stay behind. Nobody can leave the world. It ends early on Close, or if the caster is downed, leaves it or stops being Shirou.\n\nThen everyone goes back to the cell they were taken from. Corpses and dropped items land round the cast point.\n\nStopping or breaking the chant before the release gives the cooldown and the charge back.</description>
    <iconPath>RimArt/Trace/IconUnlimitedBladeWorks</iconPath>
    <category>AG_Genetic</category>
    <cooldownTicksRange>120000</cooldownTicksRange>
    <targetRequired>false</targetRequired>
    <hostile>false</hostile>
    <aiCanUse>false</aiCanUse>
    <groupAbility>false</groupAbility>
    <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>true</sendMessageOnCooldownComplete>
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <range>-1</range>
      <warmupTime>0.25</warmupTime>
      <drawAimPie>false</drawAimPie>
      <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetSelf>true</canTargetSelf>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimArt.CompProperties_AbilityUnlimitedBladeWorks" />
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimArt.UbwRules">
        <radiusByVerse>
          <li>6</li>
          <li>9</li>
          <li>12</li>
        </radiusByVerse>
        <verseSeconds>2</verseSeconds>
        <worldSecondsByVerse>
          <li>20</li>
          <li>25</li>
          <li>30</li>
        </worldSecondsByVerse>
        <!-- For the commands (Full Open, Pin, Draw, Arm, Intercept), which are not built yet. -->
        <swordCostSeconds>0.5</swordCostSeconds>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </AbilityDef>

  <!-- Reinforcement, the first of Shirou's three magics (docs/hero-echo.md, Shirou; the sketch is
       Tools/VfxLab/web/sketches/trace-reinforcement.js). Granted by the Shirou Echo while manifested; it costs
       no charge. Self, 0.5 s cast, then AG_TraceReinforced (AG_Trace_Hediffs.xml) for durationSecondsOverride.
       Cooldown 45 s. Every number is a placeholder. -->
  <AbilityDef>
    <defName>AG_Trace_Reinforcement</defName>
    <label>reinforcement</label>
    <description>Shirou strengthens his body and the weapon in his hand.\n\nCast time 0.5 seconds. For 20 seconds he moves 30% faster and deals 40% more melee damage.</description>
    <iconPath>RimArt/Trace/IconReinforcement</iconPath>
    <category>AG_Genetic</category>
    <cooldownTicksRange>2700</cooldownTicksRange>
    <jobDef>AG_CastTrace</jobDef>
    <targetRequired>false</targetRequired>
    <hostile>false</hostile>
    <aiCanUse>false</aiCanUse>
    <groupAbility>false</groupAbility>
    <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <range>-1</range>
      <warmupTime>0.5</warmupTime>
      <drawAimPie>false</drawAimPie>
      <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetSelf>true</canTargetSelf>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_AbilityGiveHediff">
        <compClass>CompAbilityEffect_GiveHediff</compClass>
        <hediffDef>AG_TraceReinforced</hediffDef>
        <onlyApplyToSelf>true</onlyApplyToSelf>
        <replaceExisting>true</replaceExisting>
        <durationSecondsOverride>20~20</durationSecondsOverride>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimArt.CompProperties_TraceFired" />
    </comps>
  </AbilityDef>

  <!-- Trace On, the second (docs/hero-echo.md, Shirou; the sketch is trace-on.js). Granted by the Shirou Echo
       while manifested; charge in AG_Echoes.xml. The button lists the trace library (every blade the pawn has
       studied through Origin: Blade, by weapon and material, best quality kept); the cast job puts away what the
       hand holds, then the 0.6 s warmup traces the copy. Cooldown 5 s. Every number is a placeholder. -->
  <AbilityDef>
    <defName>AG_Trace_On</defName>
    <label>trace on</label>
    <description>Pick a blade Shirou has studied. After a 0.6 second cast a copy of it is in his hand: the same weapon and material, one quality level below the best one of it he studied.\n\nA real weapon in his hand goes to his inventory first; a copy in his hand breaks. A copy breaks when it leaves his hand (dropped, disarmed, downed, another weapon equipped) and when he stops being Shirou. It cannot be hauled, sold or given away, and it is worth nothing.\n\nWeapons with powers of their own cannot be traced: persona weapons, weapons that grant abilities (Samehada, Chain Sickle, Fūma Shuriken) and a hero's own weapon (Yamato).\n\nA colonist with Origin: Blade can study more blades: select them and right-click a blade on the ground. A weapon or material not studied yet, or a better quality, is added to the list.</description>
    <iconPath>RimArt/Trace/IconTraceOn</iconPath>
    <gizmoClass>RimArt.Command_TraceOn</gizmoClass>
    <category>AG_Genetic</category>
    <cooldownTicksRange>300</cooldownTicksRange>
    <jobDef>AG_CastTrace</jobDef>
    <targetRequired>false</targetRequired>
    <hostile>false</hostile>
    <aiCanUse>false</aiCanUse>
    <groupAbility>false</groupAbility>
    <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</disableGizmoWhileUndrafted>
    <verbProperties>
      <verbClass>Verb_CastAbility</verbClass>
      <range>-1</range>
      <warmupTime>0.6</warmupTime>
      <drawAimPie>false</drawAimPie>
      <requireLineOfSight>false</requireLineOfSight>
      <targetParams>
        <canTargetSelf>true</canTargetSelf>
      </targetParams>
    </verbProperties>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimArt.CompProperties_TraceOn">
        <qualityBelow>1</qualityBelow>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </AbilityDef>

</Defs>
